# Aethel Engine — Cursor Rules

You are working on the Aethel Engine repository: a multi-agent IDE + creative studio.
These rules complement `.aethelrules` (the canonical project constraints). When in
doubt, `.aethelrules` wins.

## Repository layout (validated)
- **Real product (Next.js 14 App Router):** `cloud-web-app/web/`
- **Desktop app (Tauri 2 + Rust, FE incomplete):** `apps/studio-local/`
- **Design tokens:** `cloud-web-app/web/lib/design-tokens.ts` + `cloud-web-app/web/app/globals.css`
- **UI primitives:** `cloud-web-app/web/components/ui/`
- **Database:** Prisma at `cloud-web-app/web/prisma/schema.prisma`
- **Unused root trees (do NOT import from the web app):** `src/`, `client/`, root `lib/`,
  root `components/`, `runtime-templates/`, `cloud-admin-ia/`, `shared/`. The web app
  imports nothing from these (verified). Do not wire them back in.

## Stack
- Next.js 14 App Router (server components by default; `'use client'` only when you need
  state, effects, or event handlers).
- TypeScript strict mode is ON. No `any` in new code without a `// TODO(strict):` note.
  Never use `@ts-ignore` to silence real errors.
- Tailwind via design tokens (`var(--aethel-*)`). NEVER hard-code hex colors in TSX.
- Monaco (editor), xterm (terminal), Three/R3F (3D), Yjs (collab), Zustand (state),
  React Query/SWR (server state), Prisma + PostgreSQL + Redis (Upstash).

## Hard limits (from .aethelrules)
- **Max 500 LoC per component file.** Split before adding features above that.
- No `console.log` / `console.info` / `console.debug`. Use
  `createComponentLogger('<module>')` from `lib/observability/logger.ts`.
  (`console.warn` / `console.error` allowed only on framework-sensitive paths.)
- Every button needs an accessible name (text, `aria-label`, or `aria-labelledby`).
- Every new UI component ships a `*.stories.tsx`.
- Do NOT set `images.unoptimized: true` in `next.config.js` (Next/Image stays on).
- Project-relative paths only — never absolute OS paths.

## Refactoring discipline (IMPORTANT — learned the hard way)
The repo has many `chore: split … internals` commits that broke `tsc` by moving symbols
into sibling files without re-importing them. When you split a file:
1. After moving a function/type/class, ADD the import in every file that still uses it
   (or re-export it from the original module path to keep consumers working).
2. Watch for symbols used as VALUES vs TYPES — a `import type { X }` cannot be used as a
   value (e.g. `new X()` or `instanceof X`).
3. Run `npm run typecheck` in `cloud-web-app/web/` after EVERY split. Do not batch many
   splits before checking.

## Quality gates (run in cloud-web-app/web/ before considering work done)
- `npm run typecheck`  ← keep at 0 errors
- `npm run lint`       ← keep at 0 warnings/errors
- `npm run test`
- Relevant `npm run qa:*` gates for the area you touched.

## Anti-patterns to avoid
- New `*Shell.tsx` files (consolidate into the canonical shells instead).
- New duplicate `Chat` / `Agent` / `Nexus` components — extend the existing ones.
- Stub pages that only wrap a component for a route that has no real editor.
  (Thin route files that delegate to a real shared client, e.g.
  `StudioGroupedEditorClient`, are fine.)
- PT-BR strings in user-facing UI. Product UI is English; use i18n for translations.

## When adding a feature
1. Search for an existing component first (`components/ui`, `components/*`).
2. Extend it if it exists; otherwise create in the smallest appropriate scope.
3. Add a Storybook story for UI primitives.
